  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-5c0f82de3d40f91e": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-693",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The Pharisees were a politico-religious party among the Jews. Their origin is involved in obscurity, but it is commonly supposed that the beginning of the party dates from a time shortly after the Babylonish Captivity. A Pharisee is, literally, one who is separated; and it is tho…"
      },
      "c-5f95b869940118b4": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-696",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets."
      },
      "c-6576e8386ef01f7c": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-691",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This double invitation was customary among the wealthy in giving entertainments, and is still observed in some parts of the East. The invitation is given some little time in advance, as with us, and when the feast is ready a servant comes again with the announcement of the fact.…"
      },
      "c-734a134a0f8a908c": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-692",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "When the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding garment."
      },
      "c-998524c6691a3fc4": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-695",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The time when the Sadducees appeared as a party among the Jews is unknown. It is generally supposed that they had their origin about the same time as the Pharisees. The derivation of the name is a matter of dispute. Some derive it from the Hebrew tsedek, “righteousness,” and supp…"
      },
      "c-9cf97bc2adcf61e6": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-694",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "These Herodians were rather a political than a religious party. They were Jews who attached themselves to the political fortunes of the Herodian family, hoping thereby to promote the interests of the Jewish people. They were not very strict in observing the requirements of the Je…"
      }
    },
